  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the divergence found:\n\n**Babel side** (`packages/babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts`): the `legacy` option (or `version: \"legacy\"`) branches to `transformer-legacy.ts`; anything else routes into `createClassFeaturePlugin` (stage-3/TC39 semantics). Critically, `transformer-legacy.ts` (the ported `babel-plugin-transform-decorators-legacy`) never emits `Reflect.metadata`/`design:type` calls \u2014 it only builds `_applyDecoratedDescriptor`/`_initializerDefineProperty` helper calls. `babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` confirms Babel's TS transform is a pure type-stripper with zero decorator or metadata awareness \u2014 it only nulls out type annotations and handles `TSParameterProperty`. So Reflect metadata for NestJS DI under Babel only ever worked via a third-party plugin (e.g. `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`), not core Babel.\n\n**SWC side** (`crates/swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/mod.rs`): `decorators(Config)` also branches on `c.legacy`. The load-bearing line is the non-legacy branch: `if c.emit_metadata { unimplemented!(\"emitting decorator metadata while using new proposal\") }`. Metadata emission is wired only through the legacy path. `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` maps `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` \u2192 `legacy` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` \u2192 `emit_metadata` on that same `decorators::Config`, confirmed by the public option docs in `bindings/binding_core_wasm/src/types.rs`.\n\n**Root cause for the customer**: if their `.swcrc` sets `decoratorMetadata: true` without `legacyDecorator: true` (or omits `legacyDecorator`, which defaults false per `BoolConfig<false>`), SWC either panics or \u2014 more likely in their observed non-crashing case \u2014 the JS/TS-facing config layer silently no-ops metadata emission because the decorator pipeline resolved to the non-legacy fold, so no `Reflect.metadata` calls are ever generated, leaving Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata` calls with nothing to read. The fix is `legacyDecorator: true` + `decoratorMetadata: true` together in `jsc.transform`, mirroring Babel's `@babel/plugin-proposal-decorators` with `legacy: true` (though Babel alone still needs a metadata-emitting plugin layered on top, since neither core Babel package emits `design:*` metadata by itself).",
